{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>From the many you shall increase, and from the few you shall diminish</b> – This too is according to the opinion of our Sages (Bava Batra 122a): from the ancestral houses that inherited much, they shall give much, as He mentioned, \"according to your families\" (Numbers 33:54). But the tribes were equal in the inheritance, and even though you find in the book of Joshua (chapter 21) that the number of cities which they gave to the Levites is not equal among their tribes, this was because of the variation in the value of the cities, for some were considered more important than others, since the land was divided by valuation. Know this, for behold, they gave from Judah, Simeon, and Benjamin thirteen cities, and from the tribe of Issachar, Asher, Naphtali, and half the tribe of Manasseh thirteen, yet these latter are more numerous than the former in their population. And they gave from the tribe of Ephraim four cities, and from the tribe of Dan four cities, though the children of Dan were twice as many as the children of Ephraim."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:21.283827637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}